 R←Test_Table_001(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;Tbl;md
⍝ `GetTableRows` finds all rows of a table, no matter which of them the cursor is on
⍝ R gets one of: 0=Okay, 1=test case failed, ¯1=test case was not executed due to the "batchFlag"
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 Tbl←##.Meddy.Tables
 md←'Some text' '' '| A | B |' '|---|---|' '| 1 | 2 |' '' 'More text'
 →T.PassesIf 2 3 4≡Tbl.GetTableRows 2 md
 →T.PassesIf 2 3 4≡Tbl.GetTableRows 3 md
 →T.PassesIf 2 3 4≡Tbl.GetTableRows 4 md

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
